  <div class="section-wrapper" id="summary" >
    <div class="section-label"><h2>Summary</h2></div>
    <div class="section-content">
      <div class="cpu_description">The Apple M4 Pro with 14 CPU and 20 GPU cores is the full version of the M4 Pro and was launched in the fourth quarter of 2024. It is used in the Mac mini and in the 14- and 16-inch MacBook Pro. The chip is manufactured by TSMC in the second-generation 3 nm process (N3E); CPU, graphics, Neural Engine and memory are combined in a system-on-a-chip.<br />
<br />
The CPU consists of 10 performance cores at up to 4.51 GHz and 4 efficiency cores at up to 2.59 GHz. In Cinebench 2026, the M4 Pro scores around 661 points single-core and about 6,600 points multi-core, in Geekbench 6 around 3,940 and 22,700 points, and in MonkeyBench around 13,100 multi-core points. This puts it at the top in single-core performance, and in multi-core it reaches the level of fast desktop processors with 16 to 20 cores at a fraction of the power consumption.<br />
<br />
The 20-core graphics reach around 8 TFLOPS of FP32 performance and support hardware ray tracing, mesh shading and dynamic caching. With MetalFX, many games run smoothly under macOS in WQHD at high details, such as Cyberpunk 2077 or Baldur's Gate 3. Performance is roughly on the level of a mid-range laptop graphics card. However, the selection of games on macOS remains smaller than on Windows.<br />
<br />
For AI, the M4 Pro has a 16-core Neural Engine with around 38 TOPS that powers Apple Intelligence. For local language models, the memory bandwidth of 273 GB/s is crucial. With up to 64 GB of unified memory, even larger models can be run directly on the GPU that would not run on many graphics cards due to insufficient video memory.<br />
<br />
The LPDDR5X memory is available with 24, 48 or 64 GB. There is also Thunderbolt 5 with up to 120 Gbit/s for fast external SSDs, docks and up to three external displays.<br />
<br />
All in all, the Apple M4 Pro with 14 CPU and 20 GPU cores is an extremely fast and efficient chip for software development, photo and video editing, 3D and local AI. Especially in the Mac mini, it offers a very good balance of performance, size and power consumption.<ul><li>Advanced 3-nm manufacturing and M4 architecture</li><li>Powerful 14-core CPU and 20-core GPU</li><li>High computing power (Cinebench 2024: 176 Single-Core, 1742 Multi-Core)</li><li>Robust memory bandwidth of 273 GB/s</li></ul> </div>
    </div>
    
  </div>
  



